---
import CronApp from "../../components/CronApp.astro";
import ToolDiscovery from "../../components/ToolDiscovery.astro";
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import { guides } from "../../data/discovery.js";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="When will this cron run?"
  description="Read your cron expression and preview the next five runs or a clock-change week."
  seoDescription={guides["cron-explainer"].description}
  searchTitle={guides["cron-explainer"].title}
  slug="cron-explainer"
>
  <CronApp />
  <ToolDiscovery slug="cron-explainer" />
  <details class="prose tool-help">
    <summary>Supported syntax, timezones &amp; limits</summary>
    <h2>Five fields, no guessing</h2>
    <p>
      Use minute, hour, day of month, month and day of week, in that order.
      Supports numbers, wildcards, lists, ascending ranges, steps and
      month/weekday names. Sunday can be 0 or 7. Seconds, years, macros and
      Quartz-specific syntax are not supported.
    </p>
    <h2>The scheduler's timezone is not necessarily yours</h2>
    <p>
      Both timezone fields initially use your browser timezone. Change the
      schedule timezone to the one configured on your server, then choose where
      to display the same instants. This tool does not inspect or change your
      server. Run times include dates and UTC offsets so timezone changes are
      visible.
    </p>
    <h2>Preview, not an execution guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      Next five runs starts strictly after the calculation time, with a bounded
      32-year search for sparse schedules such as leap days. Selected week shows
      every occurrence over seven calendar days from your chosen date in the
      schedule timezone, including the starting midnight and excluding the next
      week's midnight. A clock-change week may be shorter or longer than 168
      hours. Weeks with no occurrences are shown explicitly. Dense previews
      display 100 runs at a time; copy and download include every occurrence.
      Timezone rules come from your browser, and actual scheduler behavior can
      differ at daylight-saving transitions. Review the result notes and your
      scheduler's documentation. Nothing is installed, scheduled, uploaded or
      saved by this tool.
    </p>
  </details>
</UtilityLayout>
